 and national culture is just a relic of the past.\n\nWoke Policies: Under Trudeau, Canada saw an explosion of DEI (Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion) initiatives that critics argue are racist in reverse, prioritizing certain groups over others under the guise of equality. These policies have infiltrated every aspect of Canadian life, from the workplace to schools, fostering division rather than unity.\n\nEconomic Mismanagement: The Canadian dollar has been in free fall, and the middle class has felt the squeeze like never before. Trudeau\'s economic strategies have been criticized for favoring globalist corporations over small businesses, leading to a significant drop in the quality of life for many Canadians.\n\nThe Tides of Change:\n\nThis resignation comes on the heels of a monumental shift in the United States. After Americans decisively voted against the globalist Democrats and Kamala Harris, the ripple effects are now felt globally. The world is waking up. The defeat of the woke agenda in the U.S. has inspired similar actions worldwide, with leaders like Trudeau finding their positions untenable as public sentiment turns against their policies.\n\nWhat This Means for Canada and Beyond:\n\nTrudeau\'s exit isn\'t just about one man leaving office; it\'s a signal that the globalist era might be coming to an end. His policies were part of a broader strategy by the likes of the World Economic Forum to reshape nations in their image. But with Trudeau stepping down, Canada has a chance to reclaim its identity, protect its borders, and restore economic policies that put its citizens first.\n\nA Call to Action:\n\nNow is the time for Canadians to demand a leader who will dismantle Trudeau\'s legacy of division and economic decline. A leader who will stand against the globalist puppeteers pulling the strings from afar. The fight isn\'t over; it\'s just beginning. We must remain vigilant, ensure that the next leader isn\'t just another face of the same globalist coin, and work towards a Canada that values its heritage, its people, and true equality over the divisive DEI policies.\n\nIn Conclusion:\n\nTrudeau\'s resignation is not just a win for Canada; it\'s a beacon of hope for all nations under the thumb of globalist control. Let this be a lesson that when the people stand united, even the most entrenched political figures can be ousted.\n\nStay tuned, keep fighting for freedom, and remember, the globalists are on the run. Let\'s keep pushing until they\'re out of power for good.', 'entity_set': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'timestamps': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': []}, 'richtext': {'richtext_tags': []}, 'media': {'inline_media': []}}}}, 'legacy': {'bookmark_count': 1, 'bookmarked': False, 'created_at': 'Mon Jan 06 16:30:03 +0000 2025', 'conversation_id_str': '1876305237935276433', 'display_text_range': [0, 277], 'entities': {'hashtags': [], 'media': [{'display_url': 'pic.x.com/UZLTO36I7S', 'expanded_url': 'https://x.com/ThomasPaineBand/status/1876305237935276433/video/1', 'id_str': '1876304600791195656', 'indices': [278, 301], 'media_key': '7_1876304600791195656', 'media_url_https': 'https://pbs.twimg.com/ext_tw_video_thumb/1876304600791195656/pu/img/-7bNSdt_c4rRRFV0.jpg', 'type': 'video', 'url': 'https://t.co/UZLTO36I7S', 'additional_media_info': {'monetizable': False}, 'ext_media_availability': {'status': 'Available'}, 'sizes': {'large': {'h': 480, 'w': 854, 'resize': 'fit'}, 'medium': {'h': 480, 'w': 854, 'resize': 'fit'}, 'small': {'h': 382, 'w': 680, 'resize': 'fit'}, 'thumb': {'h': 150, 'w': 150, 'resize': 'crop'}}, 'original_info': {'height': 480, 'width': 854, 'focus_rects': []}, 'allow_download_status': {'allow_download': True}, 'video_info': {'aspect_ratio': [427, 240], 'duration_millis': 177516, 'variants': [{'content_type': 'application/x-mpegURL', 'url': 'https://video.twimg.com/ext_tw_video/1876304600791195656/pu/pl/RJjwZrDsWzgzZjo3.m3u8?tag=12&v=3db'}, {'bitrate': 256000, 'content_type': 'video/mp4', 'url'